From: thecorporatetractor <marco@azarguard.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:11:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/16] core: make-series infers from/to when omitted

'make-series n=count() on TimeGenerated step 1h' (no from/to) failed with
"make-series requires an explicit 'from'". As in ADX, an omitted 'from' is
the first bin holding data, bin(min(axis), step), and an omitted 'to'
(exclusive) is just past the last one, bin(max(axis), step) + step. The range
comes from the whole input, so every 'by' group shares one axis. Bins align to
zero (0 ticks for datetime/timespan) like bin(). Either bound may be given on
its own; an input with no axis values yields no rows.
---
 ...TreeEvaluator.QueryOperators.MakeSeries.cs | 64 +++++++++++++++++--
 .../IRMakeSeriesOperatorNode.cs               | 18 +++---
 .../Translation/IRTranslator.MakeSeries.cs    | 10 +--
 test/BasicTests/MakeSeriesOperatorTests.cs    | 41 ++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 115 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

